<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Native AOT keeps only what it can see being used. Neo4j.Driver 6.3.0 builds its table of server-error exceptions at
  run time: Neo4jExceptionFactory reflects over the exported Neo4jException types, reads their ErrorCode attribute and
  invokes each one's non-public (FailureMessage, Exception) constructor. Those constructors are never called directly,
  so trimming removed them; the factory then threw inside a type initializer, and every server-side error (wrong
  password, constraint, syntax, transaction timeout) surfaced as TypeInitializationException in the native build
  (gate test test_wrong_password_is_reported_as_authentication, 20 November 2026).

  Keeping the driver's public namespace whole keeps those types, attributes and constructors. It does not silence the
  analysis warnings (IL2026, IL2080 on Neo4jExceptionFactory); the gate's store-failure tests are the evidence.

  AgentMemory.Neo4j passes many Cypher parameters as anonymous objects (new { limit = ... }); the driver turns an
  object parameter into a map by reflecting over its runtime type's properties. Trimming does not keep anonymous types'
  property metadata, so in the native build those parameters reached Neo4j empty ("Expected parameter(s): limit" from
  the schema bootstrap, native write probe, 20 November 2026: bug B6). The compiler puts anonymous types in the
  assembly's root namespace, so keeping that namespace keeps every anonymous parameter type with its properties,
  without changing a call site or a managed host (keeping the whole assembly worked too, 0.8 MB larger). The driver's
  converter also needs the generic instantiations in Neo4jDriver.rd.xml. The write probe (native/gate/run-write-probe.sh)
  is the evidence. Together they add about 5 MB to the library (14.8 to 20.2 MB); converting the write paths' call sites
  to dictionaries would avoid the driver's object converter and that cost.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="Neo4j.Driver">
    <namespace fullname="Neo4j.Driver" />
  </assembly>
  <assembly fullname="AgentMemory.Neo4j">
    <namespace fullname="" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
